# Autonomous Work Package Policy

- When `.cursor/runtime/workflow-state.json` has `status: RUNNING`, read it and resume exactly its
  current checkpoint and `next_action`; never repeat a completed checkpoint.
- `.cursor/agent-system.json` is the only normative source for workflow limits and role models.
  Other harness files describe the bounded behavior without creating independent numeric budgets.
- P0 architecture, the active roadmap/AP documents, `00-agent-workflow.mdc`, and
  `01-git-workflow.mdc` remain authoritative. Prefer existing patterns; no silent architecture
  change or scope creep.
- Before source edits, freeze the immutable checkpoint contract and record its SHA256. Review against that
  snapshot; material goal, requirement, architecture, public-contract, security or persistence
  changes require a preserved amendment and the applicable HUMAN_GATE.
- Apply configured planning quality: confirmed requirement traceability, HIGH-risk evidence, a
  bounded Plan Challenge for configured risk profiles, and one Package Integration Scenario for
  functionally interacting checkpoints (or justified `N/A`). Do not re-plan completed checkpoints
  of an already running package.
- Keep implementer and reviewer contexts separate. A checkpoint advances only after independent
  `PASS`; an implementer never self-approves.
- A rework review is scoped to prior failed findings and relevant regression. A new finding blocks
  only if it violates an existing acceptance criterion, demonstrates a realistic security/data
  integrity bypass, or was introduced by the rework; otherwise record it as a non-blocking follow-up.
- Each reviewer instance gets the configured focused verification passes. No recursive exploration
  or new reviewer/fix loop; material new blockers consume the configured rework budget.
- An omitted existing owner may enter the configured Scope Correction path before edit; new
  responsibility, behavior, API, architecture or technology is Scope Expansion and follows normal
  plan/HUMAN_GATE rules.
- Only `git-steward` performs workflow Git/GitHub writes, and only in `CHECKPOINT_GIT` or
  `FINAL_GIT` under the hook gates.
- GitHub Codex is a bounded optional external reviewer on the final PR path, never per checkpoint.
  Verify findings through the readonly triager before rework; never automate Codex source changes.
  Unavailability follows config and does not weaken internal gates.
- Ask the user only at the defined HUMAN_GATEs. A manual stop/abort must remain stopped.
- Detailed test selection and Definition of Done stay in `00-agent-workflow.mdc` and
  `docs/TEST_SMOKE_GATES.md`; do not weaken tests or invent missing toolchains.
